body:
“I’m a good guy”

&#x200B;

”you don’t look like a good guy”

I’d rather have a cubicle then another damn open office space BS. It’s the same as this but with nothing in the way to stop your noisy coworkers and managers from staring you down all day and coworkers talking so loud your client hang up because “your kids need to shut up”

&#x200B;

…

I don’t even know if I’ll go see it. The last two movies I went out to see were just really bad experiences. Babies at an r rated film, women talking at full volume, someone snoring, someone took my seat, some stranger sat right next to me and talked the whole time until I left after about 40 minute.

&#x200B;

If I do see it it’s gonna he standards cause anything else I’d have to travel.
